From 29770f25259b67283836bea9af228c7c66ccf020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:07:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Amazon/Meta backend: a paused company is never requested;
 adapter fixes; synthetic boards

- server/companies.js: PAUSING doc and crawlBlock(source, board); `paused` stays the one switch.
- amazon.js / meta.js: refuse to start (code 'paused') before any request while paused, whoever
  calls them (snapshot.js <slug>, fetchLive, the probe).
- probe-bigtech.js: recon/full skip paused companies; raw refuses their career hosts.
- amazon.js: pay row by whole city + state, else the job's own country, else the first row;
  each partition stops on its own `hits`; a crawl under 95% of the facet total is refused
  (a partial board would close postings in the ledger); search errors checked first.
- meta.js: no page-data anchor = JSON-LD only (plus public_compensation); addressCountry
  names normalised; sitemap lastmod kept; stop after 10 failed pages in a row; >5% failed fails.
- test/amazon-meta-synth.js: synthetic amazon.jobs / metacareers.com built from the fixtures
  (no network), plus a CLI that crawls them with the real pipeline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
